Messaging engine
=========================

## In 30 seconds

The **Notifier** is JRebirth's event bus on **JIT**. Components **listen** to `WaveType`s during `initModel` / `initService` / `initCommand`, then **sendWave** to notify others. No direct references between Models and Services are required.

## How to use

1. Define `WaveType` and `WaveItem` constants (see [Wave](Wave.html) page).
2. In the listener, call `listen(MyWaves.DO_SOMETHING)` inside the right `initXxx()` method.
3. Add a handler method (`doSomething(...)`) matching the wave contract, ending with `Wave wave`.
4. From any component, dispatch with `sendWave(MyWaves.DO_SOMETHING, WBuilder.waveData(MyWaves.ITEM, data))`.
5. Call `unlisten(...)` when the component no longer needs those events (Models are auto-unlistened on release).

JRebirth provides its own event bus to manage asynchronous communication between all components.
Synchronous communication can be achieved by using direct method call.

